   "title": "Cao Cao reaches the Yangtze",
   "time": "Autumn-winter 208",
   "narrative": "After taking Jingzhou without a fight, Cao Cao's northern army came down the river towards Jiangling and on to the Yangtze, sick and tired from forced marches. Sun Quan and Liu Bei had agreed to stand together. Their fleet and Zhou Yu's troops waited downstream on the south bank, while Cao Cao gathered his fleet of captured Jingzhou ships and his foot and horse near Wulin. The exact stretch of river is argued over, so every position here is a reconstruction.",
