  {
   "id": "aftermath",
   "title": "A divided Jingzhou",
   "time": "209-210",
   "narrative": "Zhou Yu took Jiangling by the end of 209, and Cao Cao's border shrank by some 160 km towards Xiangyang. Liu Qi died within months, and Liu Bei claimed Jingzhou, taking four commanderies south of the Yangtze. Zhou Yu died in 210. The victory fixed the split between north and south and made possible the later Three Kingdoms.",
